class.description:
[KomsoftGw] is an autoload-style singleton that talks to a KomSoft Gateway backend's leaderboard API over HTTP. It holds the connection config and exposes every action (submit, rank, top, distribution, friends). Because it is a singleton, you can call it from any script without holding a reference. [b]Pumping.[/b] Every call is [i]queued[/i] and is only issued and polled while something pumps the singleton. Add one [KomsoftGwNode] to your scene tree — it calls [method pump] each frame — and all queued work progresses. You can also call [method pump] yourself if you drive processing manually. [method pending_count] reports how many requests are queued or in flight. [b]Asynchronous results.[/b] Each action completes through a signal ([signal score_submitted], [signal rank_received], …) or [signal request_failed] on error. Actions never return data directly. [b]Authentication.[/b] Exactly like the chat API, every call is authenticated with a per-user API key. Obtain a key from the gateway first ([code]POST /v1/request-api-key[/code] with [code]{user_id, service}[/code] — typically the app already holds this key for chat) and pass it to [method configure]. Calls without a valid key for the configured [code]user_id[/code]/[code]service[/code] pair fail with [signal request_failed] code [code]401[/code]. The client automatically attaches the headers the gateway requires ([code]User-Agent[/code], [code]X-Client-Version[/code], [code]x-api-key[/code]). [b]Board types.[/b] One backend storage model drives several read projections. A board's visibility decides whether open browsing is allowed; the method you call decides what is exposed: [method get_rank] (private "you are #47 of 1,240" plus optional neighbors), [method get_distribution] (percentile bands / histogram with no names), [method get_top] (public browsable top-N), and [method get_friends] (ranking filtered to a set of friend ids). [codeblock] func _ready(): add_child(KomsoftGwNode.new()) # required: drives the queue KomsoftGw.set_use_ssl(true) # user_id is the gateway identity: "<9-char-id> <display name>". KomsoftGw.configure("https://api.example.com", "pingpal", api_key, "abc123xyz Alice") KomsoftGw.connect("score_submitted", self, "_on_submitted") KomsoftGw.connect("request_failed", self, "_on_failed") KomsoftGw.submit_score("weekly_highscore", 4200, {"level": 7})
func _on_submitted(result): print("You are rank %d of %d" % [result.rank, result.total])
func _on_failed(endpoint, code, message): push_error("%s failed (%d): %s" % [endpoint, code, message]) [/codeblock]
